  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>For questions 1 – 5, solve each quadratic equation by rewriting it in factored form and using the zero product property.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="39ac4015-3c0f-469f-9d92-50f25665caf2"><problem><para>
      <para>\(x^2 + 11x + 35 = 7\)</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(x = -4\) and \(x = -7\)</para><para>\(x = -6\) and \(x = -7\)</para><para>\(x = 14\) and \(x = -3\)</para><para>\(x = -5\) and \(x = -7\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(x = -4\) and \(x = -7\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(x = -4\) and \(x = -7\).
      </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
